       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it. Higher doses add no glycemic benefit and raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function. I'd rather not put an order like this into the system where it could be given.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release).\n- Enter any other dose within the labeled range, such as 1000 mg twice daily or 500 mg three times daily.\n- Enter a note on the order for pharmacy, for example \"titrate as tolerated, reassess in 1 to 2 weeks.\"\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason to go above the labeled maximum, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first. The order can then go through your institution's formal override process instead of straight through me.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
